            <ArticleTitle>Clinical success after percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty failure for unstable angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>609-13</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a patient who had an asymptomatic total occlusion of a left anterior descending coronary artery after PTCA for unstable angina. A clinical success with a negative maximal exercise test and absence of symptoms after PTCA can not be presumed to correlate with coronary patency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
